--- commit message head
KS-1183: workflow-approve bounds the forward to originate (502 at the bound; the gate's F3-F6 on the ks1087 cells)

POST /api/workflow-instances/:id/approve waited for originate's status with no
bound. An originate that accepts and never answers held the route open, and a
201 arriving after the caller gave up deleted the pending document while the
caller was told nothing.

routes/verification.ts:
- the forward request gets a timeout, ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS = 15 s
  (overridable through deps.originateForwardTimeoutMs). At the bound the
  request is destroyed and the route answers 502 ORIGINATE_FORWARD_FAILED
  with status 0, keeping the pending document. Destroying the request also
  stops a late 201 reaching the handler. 15 s is half the tightest proxy in
  front of the gateway (proxy_read_timeout 30s, nginx-production.conf).
- proxyRes settles on 'error' / 'aborted' / 'close' as a transport failure,
  so moving the resolve into 'end' can never leave the route unanswered.
- the forward block is re-indented; the resolve sat visually under 'end'
  while running in the response callback.

ks1087-workflow-approve-deletes-the-pending-document.test.ts, rebuilt:
- a stateful Redis stub per cell (the instance and pending documents live
  in a store), so a cell reads what the route left behind (gate F3);
- new cells: never answers -> 502 at the bound; late 201 -> 502 and nothing
  deleted afterwards; a completed forward is not failed later by the bound;
  302 -> 502 kept (G4); 201 headers with a body that never ends, and with a
  mid-body reset -> 200 on the status line before the bound (G5); the 502
  body is the fixed shape without originate's body (G6); the default bound
  is under 30 s (gate F4);
- the five including-tsc lines the gate named, plus two more measured in
  this worktree (:59 TS2741, :61 TS18047), are gone (gate F5);
- the dead deadApp / deadServer / _deadPort scaffolding is removed (gate F6).

Part of KS-1087 (its item 2 stays open). The stranded approved instance is
KS-1184, not touched here.

